1
00:00:00,880 --> 00:00:04,060
Most people use their airline benefits to see the world.

2
00:00:05,380 --> 00:00:09,860
Police say this flight attendant used hers to rob a 75-year-old grandmother.

3
00:00:10,320 --> 00:00:13,420
A 75-year-old woman answers her telephone.

4
00:00:14,480 --> 00:00:19,140
Somebody claiming to represent Publishers Clearing House tells her she's won a prize.

5
00:00:19,680 --> 00:00:25,850
She's got to send a $500 gift card to a woman named Destiny Blake in Brooklyn, New York.

6
00:00:25,900 --> 00:00:30,140
Destiny Blake, a 24-year-old American Airlines flight attendant,

7
00:00:30,360 --> 00:00:36,520
allegedly uses her employee travel privileges to fly standby from New York to Daytona Beach.

8
00:00:36,940 --> 00:00:42,190
A family member later discovered a handwritten note instructing the elderly woman to tell the

9
00:00:42,240 --> 00:00:44,980
credit card company that Blake was her granddaughter.

10
00:00:46,120 --> 00:00:49,980
Her granddaughter, by the time investigators finished putting the pieces together,

11
00:00:50,620 --> 00:00:53,860
the estimated damage was 25,310.

12
00:00:54,540 --> 00:00:58,520
Now fast forward to October 23, 2026.

13
00:00:59,680 --> 00:01:03,760
Blake lands at Miami International Airport on an international flight.

14
00:01:04,560 --> 00:01:06,290
But this time?

15
00:01:06,340 --> 00:01:07,710
Customs is waiting.

16
00:01:07,760 --> 00:01:11,220
Flagler County Sheriff Rick Staly had a few words about the case.

17
00:01:12,300 --> 00:01:13,710
Her wings were clipped.

18
00:01:13,760 --> 00:01:15,560
The charges remain allegations.

19
00:01:16,020 --> 00:01:19,090
And she is presumed innocent unless proven guilty.

20
00:01:19,140 --> 00:01:21,400
These are relentless times.

21
00:01:22,480 --> 00:01:26,140
And sometimes the most dangerous people don't come knocking with a weapon.

22
00:01:27,020 --> 00:01:31,040
They show up with a smile, a story, and a boarding pass.
